        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Fix Ollama incomplete stream model fallback",
        "body": "Closes #100460.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nAn Ollama stream that ends without a final response currently bubbles up as generic `LLM request failed.` and retries the same broken Ollama candidate instead of classifying the provider failure and advancing to configured fallback models.\n\n## Evidence\n\nConfirmed with an isolated live repro: a local mock Ollama `/api/chat` returned one incomplete NDJSON chunk and closed. Before this patch, OpenClaw made four Ollama attempts, never called the fallback endpoint, and returned `LLM request failed.` After this patch, the same repro made one Ollama request, called the configured fallback endpoint, and returned `fallback-ok`.\n\nAdded focused regression coverage for assistant failover classification and embedded result payload classification.",
